+# Receipts stopped
+
+For the volunteer on call when members say their receipt emails have stopped arriving. Restarts the worker that
+sends them and clears the receipts waiting in its queue; while it is down, members get no receipt for orders they
+have paid. Written after it happened twice: the first time nobody on call knew what to do and members waited until
+noon, and on September 14 Tomás found the worker dead since the deploy of the night before. Owner: Tomás.
+
+## Before you begin
+
+- A shell on the server where larder runs, with a checkout of this repository.
+- Rights to run `sudo systemctl` and `psql larder` there.
+- Background: receipts are jobs in a queue in Postgres, sent by the worker, the `larder-worker` service
+  ([architecture](../architecture.md#parts)). The deploy script restarts only the web app, so a deploy can leave the
+  worker stopped.
+
+## Steps
+
+1. Run `scripts/restart-receipts-worker.sh`. It checks the worker, counts the waiting jobs, starts the worker, then
+   checks the queue every 30 seconds.
+
+   Expected: the status says `inactive (dead)`, the count shows jobs in `todo` (212 on September 14), and after the
+   start the `todo` count goes down, about 40 a minute, until the script ends with `Done: no jobs waiting.`
+2. Ask a member who was missing a receipt whether it has arrived.
+
+   Expected: it has.
+
+Jobs in `failed` are not retried. On September 14 the 3 failed jobs were bounced emails to members with no valid
+address, and were left as they were.
+
+## If it fails
+
+- The script says the worker is running: the worker is not the cause. Read its log with
+  `journalctl -u larder-worker -n 50` and call Tomás.
+- The worker stops again after the start, or the `todo` count stops going down: the script prints the last 50 lines
+  of the worker's log. Keep them and call Tomás.
+- The script stops with `Failed:`: the command it names did not work, often a missing permission. Fix that and run
+  the script again; it is safe to rerun.
